# Shell scripts

- Start new shell scripts with a Bash shebang and strict mode (`pipefail` is not available in every `/bin/sh`). Keep the shebang of existing scripts: a zsh or POSIX `sh` script may rely on that shell or run where Bash is not installed:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -o errexit  # exit when a command fails
set -o pipefail # fail when a command in a pipe fails
set -o nounset  # fail when an unset variable is used
```

- Put the main logic in a `main` function at the top and call `main "$@"` on the last line, so helpers can be defined below it
- Make sure that shell scripts also work when file names contain spaces
- Prefer commands that work on Linux, MacOS and Windows WSL